    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0535" n="529" xml:id="pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/20011: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuibyshev</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-03-07T13:00:00+03:00">March 7, 1942—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>196. Embassy’s 14, January 5, 4 p.m. British Chargé d’Affaires<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d435-f1"/> has informed me that the Soviet Government has recently
                    become somewhat insistent in its efforts to obtain recognition by the British
                    Government of Soviet sovereignty over the Baltic States. I inferred that when
                    Eden endeavored to parry Maisky’s representations on the subject by citing the
                    British commitment to the United States with respect to territorial adjustments
                    Maisky urged that our Government be consulted at once.</p>
                <p>Baggallay also stated that the plan for a joint Soviet-British expedition to
                    Northern Norway was abandoned because the Soviet Government had learned that the
                    plan had become known to the Finnish Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d435-f1" n="54" xml:id="d435-f1-content">
                <p>Herbert Lacy Baggallay.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
